# Auto commit and push

After finishing an implementation task (code changes, fixes, content updates):

1. Run `npm run build` when code changed; fix failures before committing.
2. Commit with a concise message describing the why.
3. Push to `origin main` without asking the user for permission.
4. Use proxy when direct GitHub access fails:
   `git -c http.proxy=http://127.0.0.1:7897 -c https.proxy=http://127.0.0.1:7897 push origin main`
5. Report the commit hash and confirm remote matches local.

Do not ask "should I push?" — the user expects deploy-ready commits on every completed task.
